<node TEXT="Motivation and justification" ID="ID_1274895956" CREATED="1714585701965" MODIFIED="1714585710579">
<node TEXT="qualitative research: useful for exploring issues in their natural settings and through the meanings that people bring to them; researchers intend to construct meaning by foregrounding participants&apos; experiences. This is usually linked to an &quot;interpretivist orientation&quot;, which takes into account and is able to uphold multiple interpretations of reality (no one true way of seeing the world) held by the participants and the researcher. These realities are anchored in the partipants&apos; experiences and aim to capture what was particular to the specific places and times, they are socially and experientially based. However, the researcher, as the focal point of all the data, is the main filter and interpreter of those realities; they serve as witness and translator of those understandings." ID="ID_330532572" CREATED="1714584198990" MODIFIED="1714584198990" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Peel2020BeginnersGuideApplied.pdf">
<attribute NAME="key" VALUE="Peel2020BeginnersGuideApplied"/>
<attribute NAME="title" VALUE="A Beginner&apos;s Guide to Applied Educational Research using Thematic Analysis"/>
<attribute NAME="authors" VALUE="Peel, Karen L."/>
<pdf_annotation type="HIGHLIGHTED_TEXT" page="4" object_id="4067688743908369070" object_number="158"/>
</node>
</node>
<node TEXT="Concerns and criticisms" ID="ID_1027323359" CREATED="1714585447880" MODIFIED="1714585453252">
<node TEXT="concerns about qualitative analysis: credibility, transferability, dependability" ID="ID_498868906" CREATED="1714584199255" MODIFIED="1714584199255" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Mackey2005SecondLanguageResearch.pdf">
