</node>
</node>
<node TEXT="Code creation and aggregation" ID="ID_1941571870" CREATED="1714586016201" MODIFIED="1714586020931">
<node TEXT="Code list creation: ideally, labels come from actual words and behaviours present in the data. Essential to consider which are most suitable and to write comprehensive descriptions to represent them so that the connotations and meaning of the labels are made clear. The list expands iterativelly as new codes are built and former ones refined. Label descriptions are also refined and ensure accuracy in associating new extracts with code, recoding previous ones, or recognizing the need for a new code. Extracts may be suited to more than one code.&#xa;" ID="ID_188917385" CREATED="1714584199085" MODIFIED="1714584199085" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Peel2020BeginnersGuideApplied.pdf">
<attribute NAME="key" VALUE="Peel2020BeginnersGuideApplied"/>
<attribute NAME="title" VALUE="A Beginner&apos;s Guide to Applied Educational Research using Thematic Analysis"/>
<attribute NAME="authors" VALUE="Peel, Karen L."/>
<pdf_annotation type="HIGHLIGHTED_TEXT" page="9" object_id="4279744657726618719" object_number="186"/>
</node>
<node TEXT="After coding the data, the researcher has to generate code categories (*categorical aggregation*): collections of similar data sorted into types, identifying and describing the characteristics of the category, and starting to identify emerging patterns and correlations." ID="ID_1847760480" CREATED="1714584199098" MODIFIED="1714584199098" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Peel2020BeginnersGuideApplied.pdf">
