</node>
<node TEXT="Not all quantitative analyses are statistical: one can use basic arithmetic to analyze data, such as quantities: adding the number of times a theme appears to describe frequency, compare the frequencies of two themes,  talk about proportions of appearance in various subgroups of participants, etc. These operations will not tell you what the data mean, but they help summarize and describe the patterns clearly." ID="ID_1293180224" CREATED="1714584199752" MODIFIED="1714584199752" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis.pdf">
