<node TEXT="Reliability" ID="ID_918942344" CREATED="1714587053101" MODIFIED="1714587057583">
<node TEXT="Inter-rater reliability" ID="ID_514618851" CREATED="1714587015556" MODIFIED="1714587024912">
<node TEXT="summary of steps for iterative theme interpretation with inter-rater reliability checks built in to adjust and refine codes and readings:&#xa;&quot;Read the text and propose themes.&#xa;Refine the themes into codes with well-developed definitions.&#xa;Have two or more analysts read a sample of the text again and identify segments that reflect specific code definitions. (If you are the only person coding the text, you can code one sample twice, e.g., with a week between codings.)&#xa;Compare the way each analyst coded the text sample.&#xa;If the results are the same, continue coding with periodic re-checks.&#xa;If the results differ, identify why. Adjust the code definitions, the codes, or the analysts&apos; use of the codes as necessary. Recode the text as necessary. Have the analysts code another sample of text and again compare the results. Repeat as necessary.&quot;" ID="ID_1675982363" CREATED="1714584200128" MODIFIED="1714584200128" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis.pdf">
<attribute NAME="key" VALUE="Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis"/>
<attribute NAME="title" VALUE="Applied Thematic Analysis"/>
<attribute NAME="authors" VALUE="Guest, Greg and MacQueen, Kathleen and Namey, Emily"/>
<pdf_annotation type="HIGHLIGHTED_TEXT" page="83" object_id="8884119658469306936" object_number="613"/>
</node>
<node TEXT="Intercoder Agreement: the most discussed element of reliability" ID="ID_275314417" CREATED="1714584199610" MODIFIED="1714584199610" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis.pdf">
<attribute NAME="key" VALUE="Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis"/>
<attribute NAME="title" VALUE="Applied Thematic Analysis"/>
<attribute NAME="authors" VALUE="Guest, Greg and MacQueen, Kathleen and Namey, Emily"/>
<pdf_annotation type="HIGHLIGHTED_TEXT" page="106" object_id="4191132841539147541" object_number="637"/>
</node>
<node TEXT="Assessing intercoder agreement: two analysts, using the same codebook, independently tag a selected *section* of the corpus, compare their docing ans see where they agree and where their coding does not match. There are three main methods to assess it: subjective (coders review and discuss moments of disagreement without any specific structure, agree on solutions, recode, and revise if necessary); percent agreement (building on the previous method, with a tally of agreement or disagreements, and calculating a percentage; over 80% agreement is considered good); a more rigorous method is calculating a Kappa coefficient (Cohen&apos;s Kappa), 0.8 or greater is considered very good." ID="ID_910971604" CREATED="1714584199658" MODIFIED="1714584199658" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis.pdf">
<attribute NAME="key" VALUE="Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis"/>
<attribute NAME="title" VALUE="Applied Thematic Analysis"/>
<attribute NAME="authors" VALUE="Guest, Greg and MacQueen, Kathleen and Namey, Emily"/>
<pdf_annotation type="HIGHLIGHTED_TEXT" page="107" object_id="3904588278649016657" object_number="639"/>
</node>
<node TEXT="In cases where the corpus is too large and double-coding would be too expensive or time consuming, only a limited number of texts are double-coded to ensure consistency, usually more intensively at the beginning of the analysis, with less double coding as the practice becomes more stable and consistent across coders" ID="ID_578203585" CREATED="1714584199522" MODIFIED="1714584199522" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis.pdf">
<attribute NAME="key" VALUE="Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis"/>
<attribute NAME="title" VALUE="Applied Thematic Analysis"/>
<attribute NAME="authors" VALUE="Guest, Greg and MacQueen, Kathleen and Namey, Emily"/>
<pdf_annotation type="HIGHLIGHTED_TEXT" page="109" object_id="3094249291572432386" object_number="647"/>
</node>
<node TEXT="Enhancing reliability when there is only one researcher coding: do a review of the codes some time after the first one (time and perspective may help temper some biases); ask a colleague to look at a random selection of coded text with your codebook and see if the connections make sense" ID="ID_423336220" CREATED="1714584199448" MODIFIED="1714584199448" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis.pdf">
