<node TEXT="the concepts of validity and reliability vary by discipline; some researchers argue that, since the stem from quantitative research applications, they have little value for qualitative inquiry and should be replaced with others: of these, &quot;legitimacy&quot; is gaining traction, but the most common term is _credibility_, also termed _truth value_ in this context (&quot;confidence in the truth of findings, including an accurate understanding of the context&quot;). An common alternative term for &quot;reliability&quot; is _dependability_ (&quot;whether the research process is consistent and carried out with careful attention to the rules and conventions of qualitative methodology&quot;). Other scholars argue that by creating special alternative terms for qualitative research, one risks marginalizing qualitative research from mainstream science and the legitimacy with which it is associated." ID="ID_109790183" CREATED="1714584200034" MODIFIED="1714584200035" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Guest2012AppliedThematicAnalysis.pdf">
