<node TEXT="I&apos;m not that sure that a less precise CI is less informative: it just tells you a differnent thing, namely, that the reality that you are trying to measure is more spread out, there is more variability (that is a type of information!).  It may be that if you are looking for an effect to an intervention, a more spread-out CI indicates a less direct, more diffuse effect or lack of effect, but that does not necessarily make it uninformative" ID="ID_1956198220" CREATED="1557496592925" MODIFIED="1557496592925" LINK="project://16AA1F3483D6GEWV5A1JJLVG6C22R89VFR4E/../../../articulos/pedagogy/Larson-Hall2015GuideDoingStatistics.pdf">
